
PLANT DISEASED CLASSIFIER:  It is a ML model, a classifier based on Convolution Neural Network (CNN). This model is a tunned version of MobileNetV2.

How I Tunned It:
    1. Freeze only earlier layers from learning and let the last layers to learn.
    2. Make BatchNormalized layers untrainable
    3. Data Augmentation (My fav). 'Different Versions ~ flip, rotate, zoom'

This entire model is trained / tunned on a google colab. It's GPU process whole stages and train so fast.

How To Use / Run it:

    Don't forget to install all packages first:
        run: pip install pillow transformers tensorflow numpy streamlit torch

    1. Upload Datasets (Trainset.zip & Testset.zip) onto Google Drive.
    2. Name the folder Plant_Disease_Model and save both into it.
    3. Then Copy / Paste code or upload 'main_model' file on google colab and run each cell sequentially.
    4. When you run last cell of main_model file, you will get a 'plant_disease_model.keras'. 
    5. Drop it down to your root directory, where you will will clone / pull all the files in that repo.
    6. Finally, just live your app on streamlit and start serving your app.

Command to live / run the app: [streamlit run app.py]
***note: this will take some time when you start for first time...